module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.RationalEquivalence.GeometricRationalEquivalence
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Intersection.TorFormula.SectionPairFibreCycle
import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# Rational equivalence by fibres over arbitrary pairs of closed points of `ℙ¹`

Section 43.8 of the Stacks Project defines a `k`-cycle on a variety `X` to be rationally
equivalent to zero when it is a finite sum `∑ nᵢ([W_{i, aᵢ}]ₖ - [W_{i, bᵢ}]ₖ)`, where each
`Wᵢ ⊆ X × ℙ¹` is a closed subvariety of dimension `k + 1` and `aᵢ, bᵢ` is an *arbitrary* pair of
distinct closed points of `ℙ¹` such that `X × aᵢ`, `X × bᵢ` and `Wᵢ` intersect properly. Tag 0AZI
says that the principal divisors `div_W(f)` of nonzero rational functions on `(k + 1)`-dimensional
subvarieties `W ⊆ X` are rationally equivalent to zero in this sense, and that they generate the
group of cycles rationally equivalent to zero.

`Stacks.Chow.rationalEquivalencesByFibres` is the subgroup generated by the differences at the
single pair `(0, ∞)`. This file defines the subgroup generated by the differences at all pairs of
distinct closed points, `Stacks.Chow.rationalEquivalencesByClosedPoints`, identifies it with the
group `Stacks.Chow.rationalEquivalences` of Chow homology, and proves Tag 0AZI for it.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Chow.closedPointFibreDifferences` — the differences `[W_a]ₖ - [W_b]ₖ` over all pairs of
  distinct closed points `a`, `b` of `ℙ¹`.
* `Stacks.Chow.rationalEquivalencesByClosedPoints` — the group of `k`-cycles they generate.
* `Stacks.Chow.principalDivisorCycles` — the principal divisors `div_W(f)`, read as `k`-cycles.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Chow.rationalEquivalences_eq_rationalEquivalencesByClosedPoints` — the group of Section
  43.8 is the group of Chow homology.
* `Stacks.Chow.rationalEquivalencesByClosedPoints_eq_rationalEquivalencesByFibres` — the
  traditional pair `0`, `∞` gives the same group.
* `Stacks.Chow.closure_principalDivisorCycles_eq_rationalEquivalences` — on a variety the principal
  divisors generate the group of Chow homology (finite sums suffice).
* `Stacks.Chow.principalDivisorCycles_subset_and_closure_eq_rationalEquivalencesByClosedPoints` —
  **Stacks 0AZI.**

## Implementation notes

A closed point `a` of `ℙ¹` enters as a point of the topological space of `ℙ¹_S` with `{a}` closed,
and `X × a` as the image of `Stacks.Chow.closedPointSection`; the fibre `W_a`, viewed as a closed
subscheme of `X`, is the scheme-theoretic preimage of `W` along that section. Proper intersection
of an integral `W` of relative dimension `k + 1` with `X × a` is expressed, as in
`Stacks.Chow.fibreDifferences`, by asking that `W` not be contained in `X × a`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AZG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AZG)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AZI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AZI)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace

universe u

namespace Stacks.Chow

/-! ### The zero and infinity sections are sections at closed points -/

/-- Every section of `ℙ¹_S ⟶ S`, for `S` the spectrum of an algebraically closed field, is the
section at a closed point of `ℙ¹_S`, namely at the point it hits. -/
theorem exists_closedPointLineSection_eq (Kf : Type u) [Field Kf] [IsAlgClosed Kf]
    {S : Scheme.{u}} (hS : S = AlgebraicGeometry.Spec (CommRingCat.of Kf))
    (σ : S ⟶ relativeProjectiveLine S) (hσ : σ ≫ (relativeProjectiveLine S ↘ S) = 𝟙 S) :
    ∃ (a : relativeProjectiveLine S) (ha : IsClosed ({a} : Set (relativeProjectiveLine S))),
      closedPointLineSection Kf hS a ha = σ := by
  subst hS
  refine ⟨σ (IsLocalRing.closedPoint Kf),
    ((pointEquivClosedPoint (relativeProjectiveLine _ ↘ _)) ⟨σ, hσ⟩).2, ?_⟩
  exact ext_of_apply_closedPoint_eq (relativeProjectiveLine _ ↘ _)
    (closedPointLineSection_comp Kf rfl _ _) hσ (closedPointLineSection_apply Kf rfl _ _ _)

/-- Over the spectrum of an algebraically closed field the zero section of `X ×_S ℙ¹_S ⟶ X` is
the section at a closed point of `ℙ¹_S`. -/
theorem exists_closedPointSection_eq_zeroSection (Kf : Type u) [Field Kf] [IsAlgClosed Kf]
    {X S : Scheme.{u}} (hS : S = AlgebraicGeometry.Spec (CommRingCat.of Kf)) (f : X ⟶ S) :
    ∃ (a : relativeProjectiveLine S) (ha : IsClosed ({a} : Set (relativeProjectiveLine S))),
      closedPointSection Kf hS a ha f = zeroSection f := by
  obtain ⟨a, ha, h⟩ :=
    exists_closedPointLineSection_eq Kf hS (lineZeroSection S) (lineZeroSection_comp S)
  refine ⟨a, ha, pullback.hom_ext ?_ ?_⟩
  · rw [closedPointSection_comp_fst, zeroSection_comp_fst]
  · rw [closedPointSection_comp_snd, zeroSection_comp_snd, h]

/-- Over the spectrum of an algebraically closed field the infinity section of
`X ×_S ℙ¹_S ⟶ X` is the section at a closed point of `ℙ¹_S`. -/
theorem exists_closedPointSection_eq_infinitySection (Kf : Type u) [Field Kf] [IsAlgClosed Kf]
    {X S : Scheme.{u}} (hS : S = AlgebraicGeometry.Spec (CommRingCat.of Kf)) (f : X ⟶ S) :
    ∃ (a : relativeProjectiveLine S) (ha : IsClosed ({a} : Set (relativeProjectiveLine S))),
      closedPointSection Kf hS a ha f = infinitySection f := by
  obtain ⟨a, ha, h⟩ :=
    exists_closedPointLineSection_eq Kf hS (lineInfinitySection S) (lineInfinitySection_comp S)
  refine ⟨a, ha, pullback.hom_ext ?_ ?_⟩
  · rw [closedPointSection_comp_fst, infinitySection_comp_fst]
  · rw [closedPointSection_comp_snd, infinitySection_comp_snd, h]

/-! ### The group of Section 43.8 -/

/-- The basic rational equivalences of Section 43.8: the differences `[W_a]ₖ - [W_b]ₖ`, for `a`,
`b` an arbitrary pair of distinct closed points of `ℙ¹` and `W ⊆ X ×_S ℙ¹_S` an integral closed
subscheme of relative dimension `k + 1` contained in neither `X × a` nor `X × b`. -/
@[stacks 0AZG "the basic rational equivalences `[W_a]_k - [W_b]_k` of Section 43.8, over an \
ARBITRARY pair of distinct closed points `a`, `b` of `P^1`. A closed point is a point of `P^1` \
whose singleton is closed, `X × a` is the image of `Stacks.Chow.closedPointSection`, and the \
fibre `W_a` is the scheme-theoretic preimage of `W` along that section, viewed as a closed \
subscheme of `X` as the source does. Proper intersection of an integral `W` of relative \
dimension `k + 1` with `X × a` and `X × b` is expressed by asking that `W` be contained in \
neither."]
def closedPointFibreDifferences (Kf : Type u) [Field Kf] [IsAlgClosed Kf]
    (C : ChowSituation.{u}) (hC : C.S = AlgebraicGeometry.Spec (CommRingCat.of Kf))
    {X : Scheme.{u}} (p : X ⟶ C.S) [LocallyOfFiniteType p] (k : ℤ) :
    Set (CycleGroup C p k) :=
  {γ | ∃ (a b : relativeProjectiveLine C.S)
      (ha : IsClosed ({a} : Set (relativeProjectiveLine C.S)))
      (hb : IsClosed ({b} : Set (relativeProjectiveLine C.S))), a ≠ b ∧
    ∃ W : (projectiveLineProduct p).IdealSheafData,
      IsIntegral W.subscheme ∧
      (∀ ξ : genericPoints W.subscheme,
        relativeDimension C.dimensionFunction (familyBase p W) ξ.1 = k + 1) ∧
      (¬ Set.range W.subschemeι ⊆ Set.range (closedPointSection Kf hC a ha p)) ∧
      (¬ Set.range W.subschemeι ⊆ Set.range (closedPointSection Kf hC b hb p)) ∧
      γ = cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme C p
          (W.comap (closedPointSection Kf hC a ha p)).subschemeι k -
        cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme C p
          (W.comap (closedPointSection Kf hC b hb p)).subschemeι k}

/-- The group of `k`-cycles rationally equivalent to zero of Section 43.8: the subgroup of
`Zₖ(X)` generated by the differences `[W_a]ₖ - [W_b]ₖ` over all pairs of distinct closed points
of `ℙ¹`, that is, the cycles `∑ nᵢ([W_{i, aᵢ}]ₖ - [W_{i, bᵢ}]ₖ)`. -/
@[stacks 0AZG "the group of `k`-cycles rationally equivalent to zero of Section 43.8, the cycles \
`∑ nᵢ([W_{i, aᵢ}]_k - [W_{i, bᵢ}]_k)` with an ARBITRARY pair of distinct closed points \
`aᵢ`, `bᵢ` of `P^1` for each `i`, as in `Stacks.Chow.closedPointFibreDifferences`."]
def rationalEquivalencesByClosedPoints (Kf : Type u) [Field Kf] [IsAlgClosed Kf]
    (C : ChowSituation.{u}) (hC : C.S = AlgebraicGeometry.Spec (CommRingCat.of Kf))
    {X : Scheme.{u}} (p : X ⟶ C.S) [LocallyOfFiniteType p] (k : ℤ) :
    AddSubgroup (CycleGroup C p k) :=
  AddSubgroup.closure (closedPointFibreDifferences Kf C hC p k)

/-- On a variety over an algebraically closed field the group of `k`-cycles rationally
equivalent to zero of Section 43.8, built from all pairs of distinct closed points of `ℙ¹`, is
the group `Stacks.Chow.rationalEquivalences` of Chow homology. -/
theorem rationalEquivalences_eq_rationalEquivalencesByClosedPoints (Kf : Type u) [Field Kf]
    [IsAlgClosed Kf] (C : ChowSituation.{u})
    (hC : C.S = AlgebraicGeometry.Spec (CommRingCat.of Kf)) {X : Scheme.{u}}
    (p : X ⟶ C.S) [LocallyOfFiniteType p]
    [AlgebraicGeometry.IsVariety Kf (p ≫ eqToHom hC)] (k : ℤ) :
    rationalEquivalences C p k = rationalEquivalencesByClosedPoints Kf C hC p k := by
  refine le_antisymm ?_ ?_
  · rw [rationalEquivalences_eq_rationalEquivalencesByFibres Kf C hC p k]
    refine (AddSubgroup.closure_le _).2 ?_
    rintro γ ⟨W, hW, hDim, h₀, hInf, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨a, ha, e₀⟩ := exists_closedPointSection_eq_zeroSection Kf hC p
    obtain ⟨b, hb, eInf⟩ := exists_closedPointSection_eq_infinitySection Kf hC p
    have key : ∀ s s' : X ⟶ projectiveLineProduct p, s = s' →
        cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme C p (W.comap s).subschemeι k =
          cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme C p (W.comap s').subschemeι k := by
      rintro s _ rfl
      rfl
    by_cases hab : a = b
    · subst hab
      have h0 : cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme C p (zeroFiber p W).subschemeι k -
          cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme C p (infinityFiber p W).subschemeι k = 0 :=
        sub_eq_zero.2 (key _ _ (e₀.symm.trans eInf))
      rw [h0]
      exact zero_mem _
    · refine AddSubgroup.subset_closure ⟨a, b, ha, hb, hab, W, hW, hDim, ?_, ?_, ?_⟩
      · rwa [e₀]
      · rwa [eInf]
      · exact (congrArg₂ (· - ·) (key _ _ e₀) (key _ _ eInf)).symm
  · refine (AddSubgroup.closure_le (rationalEquivalences C p k)).2 ?_
    rintro γ ⟨a, b, ha, hb, -, W, hW, hDim, hA, hB, rfl⟩
    have := hW
    exact sub_cycleAssociatedToClosedSubscheme_comap_mem_rationalEquivalences C p k
      (exists_closedPointSection_eq_pointSection_or_eq_infinitySection Kf hC a ha p)
      (exists_closedPointSection_eq_pointSection_or_eq_infinitySection Kf hC b hb p)
      W hDim hA hB

/-- **The traditional choice `a = 0`, `b = ∞` gives the same group.** On a variety over an
algebraically closed field the group of `k`-cycles rationally equivalent to zero of Section 43.8,
built from arbitrary pairs of distinct closed points of `ℙ¹`, is generated by the fibre
differences `Stacks.Chow.fibreDifferences` at the single pair `0`, `∞`. -/
@[stacks 0AZG "the remark of Section 43.8 that the pair of closed points may be moved to any \
pair we like, the traditional choice being `a = 0`, `b = ∞`: the group \
`Stacks.Chow.rationalEquivalencesByClosedPoints` built from arbitrary pairs of distinct closed \
points equals the group `Stacks.Chow.rationalEquivalencesByFibres` built from the pair `0`, \
`∞`. The source moves the pair by the 2-transitivity of the automorphism group of `P^1`; here \
the equality goes through the group of cycles rationally equivalent to zero of Chow homology, \
which both groups equal."]
theorem rationalEquivalencesByClosedPoints_eq_rationalEquivalencesByFibres (Kf : Type u)
    [Field Kf] [IsAlgClosed Kf] (C : ChowSituation.{u})
    (hC : C.S = AlgebraicGeometry.Spec (CommRingCat.of Kf)) {X : Scheme.{u}}
    (p : X ⟶ C.S) [LocallyOfFiniteType p]
    [AlgebraicGeometry.IsVariety Kf (p ≫ eqToHom hC)] (k : ℤ) :
    rationalEquivalencesByClosedPoints Kf C hC p k = rationalEquivalencesByFibres C p k := by
  rw [← rationalEquivalences_eq_rationalEquivalencesByClosedPoints Kf C hC p k,
    rationalEquivalences_eq_rationalEquivalencesByFibres Kf C hC p k]

/-! ### Principal divisors -/

/-- The principal divisors `div_V(f)` of nonzero rational functions `f` on integral closed
subschemes `V ⊆ X` of delta-dimension `k + 1`, pushed forward to `k`-cycles on `X`. -/
def principalDivisorCycles (C : ChowSituation.{u}) {X : Scheme.{u}} (p : X ⟶ C.S)
    [LocallyOfFiniteType p] (k : ℤ) : Set (CycleGroup C p k) :=
  {γ | ∃ (V : X.IdealSheafData) (hV : IsIntegral V.subscheme)
    (hDim : schemeDeltaDimension C (V.subschemeι ≫ p) = ((k + 1 : ℤ) : EInt))
    (f : (rationalFunctions V.subscheme)ˣ),
    γ = ⟨principalDivisorPushforward C p V hV f,
      principalDivisorPushforward_mem_cyclesOfDimension C p k V hV hDim f⟩}

/-- On a variety the principal divisors generate the group of `k`-cycles rationally equivalent
to zero of Chow homology: its locally finite sums of principal divisors are finite sums, since a
variety is quasi-compact. -/
theorem closure_principalDivisorCycles_eq_rationalEquivalences (Kf : Type u) [Field Kf]
    (C : ChowSituation.{u}) (hC : C.S = AlgebraicGeometry.Spec (CommRingCat.of Kf))
    {X : Scheme.{u}} (p : X ⟶ C.S) [LocallyOfFiniteType p]
    [AlgebraicGeometry.IsVariety Kf (p ≫ eqToHom hC)] (k : ℤ) :
    AddSubgroup.closure (principalDivisorCycles C p k) = rationalEquivalences C p k := by
  refine le_antisymm ?_ (fun α hα ↦ ?_)
  · refine (AddSubgroup.closure_le (rationalEquivalences C p k)).2 ?_
    rintro γ ⟨V, hV, hDim, f, rfl⟩
    rw [SetLike.mem_coe, mem_rationalEquivalences]
    refine ⟨PUnit.{u + 1}, fun _ ↦ V, fun _ ↦ hV, fun _ ↦ hDim, ?_, fun _ ↦ f, fun x ↦ ?_⟩
    · exact fun x ↦ ⟨Set.univ, Filter.univ_mem, Set.finite_univ.subset (fun j _ ↦ trivial)⟩
    · rw [principalDivisorFamilyCoefficient, finsum_unique]
  · rw [mem_rationalEquivalences] at hα
    obtain ⟨J, V, hV, hDim, hLocal, g, hCoeff⟩ := hα
    have : CompactSpace X := QuasiCompact.compactSpace_of_compactSpace (p ≫ eqToHom hC)
    have : Finite J := finite_of_locallyFinite_of_nonempty
      (fun j ↦ ((V j).support : Set X)) hLocal
      (fun j ↦ @nonempty_support_of_isIntegral _ (V j) (hV j))
    let _ : Fintype J := Fintype.ofFinite J
    set γ : J → CycleGroup C p k := fun j ↦
      ⟨principalDivisorPushforward C p (V j) (hV j) (g j),
        principalDivisorPushforward_mem_cyclesOfDimension C p k (V j) (hV j) (hDim j) (g j)⟩
      with hγdef
    have hsum : (∑ j, γ j) ∈ AddSubgroup.closure (principalDivisorCycles C p k) :=
      AddSubmonoid.sum_mem (AddSubgroup.closure (principalDivisorCycles C p k)).toAddSubmonoid
        fun j _ ↦ AddSubgroup.subset_closure ⟨V j, hV j, hDim j, g j, rfl⟩
    have hval : α = ∑ j, γ j := by
      refine Subtype.ext (Function.locallyFinsuppWithin.ext fun x ↦ ?_)
      have hrhs : ((∑ j, γ j : CycleGroup C p k) : AlgebraicCycle X ℤ) x =
          ∑ j, principalDivisorPushforward C p (V j) (hV j) (g j) x := by
        simp [hγdef]
      rw [hrhs, hCoeff x, principalDivisorFamilyCoefficient,
        finsum_eq_sum_of_support_subset _ (s := Finset.univ) (by intro j _; simp)]
    rw [hval]
    exact hsum

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0AZI.** Let `X` be a variety over an algebraically closed field, and
let `k` be an integer. The principal divisor `div_V(f)` of a nonzero rational function `f` on an
integral closed subscheme `V ⊆ X` of dimension `k + 1`, viewed as a `k`-cycle on `X`, is
rationally equivalent to zero in the sense of Section 43.8; conversely these principal divisors
generate the group of `k`-cycles rationally equivalent to zero in that sense. -/
@[stacks 0AZI "both assertions, against the group of Section 43.8 \
(`Stacks.Chow.rationalEquivalencesByClosedPoints`, generated by `[W_a]_k - [W_b]_k` over \
ARBITRARY pairs of distinct closed points `a`, `b` of `P^1`): every principal divisor `div_W(f)` \
of a nonzero rational function on a `(k + 1)`-dimensional integral closed subscheme `W ⊆ X` lies \
in it, and the subgroup these principal divisors generate is all of it. `X` is a variety over an \
algebraically closed field `Kf`; principal divisors are pushed forward to cycles on `X` as \
`Stacks.Chow.principalDivisorPushforward`, and `principal divisor` is \
`Stacks.Chow.principalDivisorCycles`."]
theorem principalDivisorCycles_subset_and_closure_eq_rationalEquivalencesByClosedPoints
    (Kf : Type u) [Field Kf] [IsAlgClosed Kf] (C : ChowSituation.{u})
    (hC : C.S = AlgebraicGeometry.Spec (CommRingCat.of Kf)) {X : Scheme.{u}}
    (p : X ⟶ C.S) [LocallyOfFiniteType p]
    [AlgebraicGeometry.IsVariety Kf (p ≫ eqToHom hC)] (k : ℤ) :
    principalDivisorCycles C p k ⊆ rationalEquivalencesByClosedPoints Kf C hC p k ∧
      AddSubgroup.closure (principalDivisorCycles C p k) =
        rationalEquivalencesByClosedPoints Kf C hC p k := by
  have h : AddSubgroup.closure (principalDivisorCycles C p k) =
      rationalEquivalencesByClosedPoints Kf C hC p k := by
    rw [closure_principalDivisorCycles_eq_rationalEquivalences Kf C hC p k,
      rationalEquivalences_eq_rationalEquivalencesByClosedPoints Kf C hC p k]
  exact ⟨h ▸ AddSubgroup.subset_closure, h⟩

end Stacks.Chow

end
